e":"1","artid":"104","page_start":"104","journal_title":"Physica"}}},{"reference":{"report_numbers":["PROC,14"]}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"202","artid":"166","page_start":"166","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"202","artid":"323","page_start":"323","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"202","artid":"336","page_start":"336","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"205","artid":"357","page_start":"357","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"205","artid":"541","page_start":"541","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"213","artid":"113","page_start":"113","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}}],"number_of_pages":18,"referenced_authors_bais":["Paul.Adrien.Maurice.Dirac.1"],"legacy_version":"20200929124034.0","legacy_creation_date":"2008-09-18","preprint_date":"1955-03-15","author_count":1,"first_author":{"full_name":"Lowdin, Per-Olov","last_name":"Lowdin","first_name":"Per-Olov","recid":2247642},"control_number":47393,"dois":[{"value":"10.1103/PhysRev.97.1490"}],"earliest_date":"1955-03-15","document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Lowdin:1955zza"],"abstracts":[{"source":"APS","value":"A system of N antisymmetric particles, moving under the influence of a fixed potential and their mutual many-particle interactions, is investigated in the ordinary Hartree-Fock scheme, having the total wave function approximated by a single Slater determinant. It is shown that all the density matrices of various orders, the wave function, and the entire physical situation depends only on a fundamental invariant ρ(x1, x2), which is identical with the first-order density matrix. The Hartree-Fock equations are expressed in terms of this quantity.\nThe Hartree-Fock equations are also solved by expanding the eigenfunctions in a given complete set, and applications to the MO-LCAO theory of the electronic structure of molecules, and crystals are given. It is shown that, in this scheme, the entire physical situation depends on a charge- and bond-order matrix R(νμ) with respect to the ordinary atomic spin-orbitals involved. The Hartree-Fock equations for this matrix are investigated.\nFinally, the ionized and excited states are investigated, and it is shown that the Hartree-Fock scheme has a high degree of physical visuality also in case of many-particle interactions. The excitation energy of the system is the difference (ωj′−ωi) between two \"spin-orbital energies,\" being eigenvalues to the effective Hamiltonians associated with the two states under consideration.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}}],"refereed":true,"titles":[{"title":"Quantum Theory of Many-Particle Systems. 2. Study of the Ordinary Hartree-Fock Approximation"}],"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"SPIRES","value":"SPIRES-7958269"}],"facet_author_name":["2247642_Per-Olov Lowdin"],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:47393","updated":"2023-03-06T14:43:56.933129"},"curated":true,"journal_title_variants":["Phys.Rev.","Phys. Rev."]},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47393?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47393?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47393?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47393?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47393?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47393?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A47393"},"created":"2008-09-18T00:00:00+00:00"},{"updated":"2026-07-25T13:43:21.821303+00:00","id":"47394","metadata":{"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"97","page_end":"1520","year":1955,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api