nfo":{"journal_volume":"201","artid":"196","page_start":"196","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"92","artid":"28","page_start":"28","journal_title":"Phys.Rev."}}},{"reference":{"misc":["Ark.Mat.Astron.Fys.,A35,"]}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"18","artid":"365","page_start":"365","journal_title":"J.Chem.Phys."}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"192","artid":"16","page_start":"16","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"report_numbers":["PROC,456"]}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"195","artid":"188","page_start":"188","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"200","artid":"542","page_start":"542","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"201","artid":"125","page_start":"125","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"206","artid":"489","page_start":"489","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"}}},{"reference":{"report_numbers":["PROC,197"]}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"21","artid":"1750","page_start":"1750","journal_title":"J.Chem.Phys."}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"1","artid":"104","page_start":"104","journal_title":"Physica"}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"91","artid":"528","page_start":"528","journal_title":"Phys.Rev."}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"20","artid":"1024","page_start":"1024","journal_title":"J.Chem.Phys."}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"43","artid":"581","page_start":"581","journal_title":"Phil.Mag."}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"11","artid":"203","page_start":"203","journal_title":"J.Chem.Phys."}}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"journal_volume":"88","artid":"1217","page_start":"1217","journal_title":"Phys.Rev."}}}],"number_of_pages":15,"referenced_authors_bais":["Eugene.P.Wigner.1","J.C.Slater.1","Paul.Adrien.Maurice.Dirac.1","F.Seitz.1"],"legacy_version":"20200929124034.0","legacy_creation_date":"2008-09-18","preprint_date":"1955-03-15","author_count":1,"first_author":{"full_name":"Lowdin, Per-Olov","last_name":"Lowdin","first_name":"Per-Olov","recid":2247642},"control_number":47392,"dois":[{"value":"10.1103/PhysRev.97.1474"}],"earliest_date":"1955-03-15","document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Lowdin:1955zzb"],"abstracts":[{"source":"APS","value":"In order to calculate the average value of a physical quantity containing also many-particle interactions in a system of N antisymmetric particles, a set of generalized density matrices are defined. In order to permit the investigation of the same physical situation in two complementary spaces, the Hermitean density matrix of order k has two sets of indices of each k variables, and it is further antisymmetric in each set of these indices.\nEvery normalizable antisymmetric wave function may be expanded in a series of determinants of order N over all ordered configurations formed from a basic complete set of one-particle functions ψk, which gives a representation of the wave function and its density matrices also in the discrete k-space. The coefficients in an expansion of an eigenfunction to a particular operator may be determined by the variation principle, leading to the ordinary secular equation of the method of configurational interaction. It is shown that the first-order density matrix may be brought to diagonal form, which defines the \"natural spin-orbitals\" associated with the system. The situation is then partly characterized by the corresponding occupation numbers, which are shown to lie between 0 and 1 and to assume the value 1, only if the corresponding spin-orbital occurs in all configurations necessary for describing the situation. If the system has exactly N spin-orbitals which are fully occupied, the total wave function may be reduced to a single Slater determinant. However, due to the mutual interaction between the particles, this limiting case is never physically realized, but the introduction of natural spin-orbitals leads then instead to a configurational expansion of most rapid convergence.\nIn case the basic set is of finite order M, the best choice of this set is determined by a form of extended Hartree-Fock equations. It is shown that, in this case, the natural spin-orbitals approximately fulfill some equations previously proposed by Slater.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}}],"refereed":true,"titles":[{"title":"Quantum Theory of Many-Particle Systems. 1. Physical Interpretations by Means of Density Matrices, Natural Spin-Orbitals, and Convergence Problems in the Method of Configurational Interaction"}],"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"SPIRES","value":"SPIRES-7958250"}],"facet_author_name":["2247642_Per-Olov Lowdin"],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:47392","updated":"2023-03-09T12:34:24.096387"},"curated":true,"journal_title_variants":["Phys. Rev.","Phys.Rev."]},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47392?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47392?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47392?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47392?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47392?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/47392?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A47392"},"created":"2008-09-18T00:00:00+00:00"}],"total":4},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=title%20%22Quantum%20Theory%20of%20Many-Particle%20Systems%22&size=10&page=1","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=title%20%22Quantum%20Theory%20of%20Many-Particle%20Systems%22&size=10&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=title%20%22Quantum%20Theory%20of%20Many-Particle%20Systems%22&size=10&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=title%20%22Quantum%20Theory%20of%20Many-Particle%20Systems%22&size=10&page=1&format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=title%20%22Quantum%20Theory%20of%20Many-Particle%20Systems%22&size=10&page=1&format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=title%20%22Quantum%20Theory%20of%20Many-Particle%20Systems%22&size=10&page=1&format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=title%20%22Quantum%20Theory%20of%20Many-Particle%20Systems%22&size=10&page=1&format=cv"}}